From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jaime Dias <jaimejosediasnt@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 17 Aug 2026 18:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 23/23] fat: read the first-cluster fields little-endian

Completes what 0006 started. That patch fixed the write side and stopped
there, deliberately: substituting the read-side raw comparisons as well had
been measured taking the boot from 3 of 6 runs to 0 of 6, so the comparison
was left alone and the reason recorded in the code. This finishes the job,
and the boundary 0006 drew is the thing being deliberately crossed.

GetDirEntryByCluster() compared the on-disk halves against a native ULONG:

    if (de->e.entry.first_cluster_hi == (cluster >> 16)
        && de->e.entry.first_cluster_lo == (cluster & 0xffff))

Those halves are little-endian on disk whatever the host is, so on a
big-endian one the test never matches. Its only caller is GetParentDir(),
and only on the branch that looks the parent up in the grandparent -- which
is entered exactly when the parent is not the root. So ParentDir() works at
one level of depth and fails at two or more, which is not a subtle failure
mode: C:Copy calls ParentDir() at Copy.c:1826 and returns silently when it
comes back NULL, so

    Copy >NIL: "ENVARC:" "ENV:" ALL NOPRO NOREQ PAT "~(def_#?.info)"

copies nothing, ENV: stays empty, and every If EXISTS "ENV:..." in the
Startup-Sequence takes the Else. No preference of any kind loads -- the
theme is only the visible half of it.

Measured before the fix, on a card generated by mcopy so the on-disk fields
are correct: Copy of S:Shell-Startup (parent one level down) works, Copy of
anything under Prefs/Env-Archive (two or more) copies nothing and says
nothing. That is the predicted boundary, not a summary of one.

Two more asymmetries go with it, because leaving them is the same defect
wearing a disguise:

  * OpRenameFile() reassembled the raw halves and handed them to
    CreateDirEntry(), which -- since 0006 -- encodes what it is given. The
    missing decode and the added encode cancelled, so the bytes on disk were
    right by accident. Decode explicitly.
  * Format() wrote bs_volid natively while the mount path decodes it, so the
    serial on the card was never the serial the volume reported.

The rest of the handler is already clean and was checked field by field:
the FAT table accessors (fat.c), the FSInfo block, the long-name UTF-16
halves (names.c), the BPB (compiler/fatbpb is byte-wise), file_size, and
the date and time words, which 0008 converts at the ConvertFATDate /
ConvertDOSDate boundary. What remains raw is field-to-field copying, which
does not interpret the value.

Upstream defect on every big-endian AROS target; m68k-amiga, ppc-native and
ppc-morphos share this code, and origin/master still carries it.

See AI_context/issues/ISSUE-0036.md.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 rom/filesys/fat/direntry.c | 13 ++++++-------
 rom/filesys/fat/ops.c      |  6 ++++--
 rom/filesys/fat/volume.c   |  6 ++++--
 3 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/rom/filesys/fat/direntry.c b/rom/filesys/fat/direntry.c
--- a/rom/filesys/fat/direntry.c
+++ b/rom/filesys/fat/direntry.c
@@ -236,11 +236,13 @@
     /* Start at the start */
     RESET_DIRHANDLE(dh);
 
-    /* Loop through the entries until we find a match */
+    /* Loop through the entries until we find a match. Decode the entry's
+     * field rather than encoding the wanted cluster: the two halves are
+     * stored little-endian on disk whatever the host is, and comparing them
+     * raw against a native value never matches on a big-endian one. */
     while ((err = GetNextDirEntry(dh, de, glob)) == 0)
     {
-        if (de->e.entry.first_cluster_hi == (cluster >> 16)
-            && de->e.entry.first_cluster_lo == (cluster & 0xffff))
+        if (FIRST_FILE_CLUSTER(de) == cluster)
         {
             D(bug("[fat] matched starting cluster at entry %ld, returning\n",
                 dh->cur_index));
@@ -580,10 +582,7 @@
 
     /* Little-endian on the way out. Upstream converts these on read
      * (FIRST_FILE_CLUSTER, lock.c) and not on write, which is a no-op on a
-     * little-endian host and a swapped field on a big-endian one.
-     * WRITE SIDE ONLY -- the read-side raw comparisons are deliberately left
-     * as upstream has them; substituting them as well is what a bisect
-     * identified as breaking the boot. See AI_context/issues/ISSUE-0007.md. */
+     * little-endian host and a swapped field on a big-endian one. */
     de->e.entry.first_cluster_lo = AROS_WORD2LE(cluster & 0xffff);
     de->e.entry.first_cluster_hi = AROS_WORD2LE(cluster >> 16);
 
diff --git a/rom/filesys/fat/ops.c b/rom/filesys/fat/ops.c
--- a/rom/filesys/fat/ops.c
+++ b/rom/filesys/fat/ops.c
@@ -595,9 +595,11 @@
      * entries for the new name, just overwrite the name */
 
     /* Make a new entry in the target dir */
+    /* CreateDirEntry() takes a native cluster number and encodes it, so hand
+     * it the decoded field rather than the raw halves. Reassembling them raw
+     * round-tripped only because the encode undid the missing decode. */
     if ((err = CreateDirEntry(&ddh, dname, dnamelen,
-        sde.e.entry.attr | ATTR_ARCHIVE,
-        (sde.e.entry.first_cluster_hi << 16) | sde.e.entry.first_cluster_lo,
+        sde.e.entry.attr | ATTR_ARCHIVE, FIRST_FILE_CLUSTER(&sde),
         &dde, glob)) != 0)
     {
         ReleaseDirHandle(&ddh, glob);
diff --git a/rom/filesys/fat/volume.c b/rom/filesys/fat/volume.c
--- a/rom/filesys/fat/volume.c
+++ b/rom/filesys/fat/volume.c
@@ -599,9 +599,11 @@
     ebpb->bs_bootsig = 0x29;
 
     /* Generate a pseudo-random serial number. Not the original algorithm,
-     * but it shouldn't matter */
+     * but it shouldn't matter. Encoded on the way out, because the mount path
+     * decodes it (AROS_LE2LONG on bs_volid above): written natively, the
+     * serial on the card is not the one this volume reports. */
     ReadEClock(&eclock);
-    ebpb->bs_volid = FastRand(eclock.ev_lo ^ eclock.ev_hi);
+    ebpb->bs_volid = AROS_LONG2LE(FastRand(eclock.ev_lo ^ eclock.ev_hi));
 
     /* Copy volume name in */
     for (i = 0; i < FAT_MAX_SHORT_NAME; i++)
